# 1️⃣ What is Recursion?

## 📖 Definition

Recursion is a process where a function repeatedly calls itself until a stopping condition (Base Case) is reached.

---

### Example

```
print(5)

↓

print(4)

↓

print(3)

↓

print(2)

↓

print(1)

↓

Stop
```

---

# 2️⃣ Structure of a Recursive Function

Every recursive function has two important parts.

### Base Case

Stops recursion.

### Recursive Case

Calls the function again with a smaller problem.

---

### General Syntax

```cpp
void recursion(int n)
{
    // Base Case
    if(n == 0)
        return;

    // Work

    recursion(n - 1);
}
```

---

# 3️⃣ Example - Print Numbers from N to 1

### C++ Code

```cpp
#include<iostream>
using namespace std;

void print(int n)
{
    if(n == 0)
        return;

    cout << n << " ";

    print(n - 1);
}

int main()
{
    print(5);
}
```

---

### Output

```
5 4 3 2 1
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(n)
```

### Space Complexity

```
O(n)
```

