# 8️⃣ Advantages of Recursion

✅ Easy to understand

✅ Short and clean code

✅ Solves complex problems naturally

✅ Useful for Trees and Graphs

✅ Essential for Backtracking

---

# 9️⃣ Disadvantages of Recursion

❌ Uses extra memory (Call Stack)

❌ Slower than iteration

❌ Stack Overflow for deep recursion

❌ Harder to debug

---

# 🔟 Iteration vs Recursion

| Feature | Iteration | Recursion |
|----------|-----------|-----------|
| Uses Loops | ✅ | ❌ |
| Function Calls | ❌ | ✅ |
| Extra Memory | O(1) | O(n) |
| Performance | Faster | Slightly Slower |
| Readability | Moderate | High |

---

# 📊 Complexity Analysis

| Operation | Complexity |
|------------|------------|
| Time | O(n) |
| Space | O(n) |

---

# 💡 Interview Tips

✅ Every recursive function must have a **Base Case**.

✅ Each recursive call should move toward the Base Case.

✅ Always dry-run recursion using the Call Stack.

✅ Recursion uses stack memory.

✅ Infinite recursion causes **Stack Overflow**.

---

# 📝 Summary

- Recursion is a function calling itself.
- Base Case stops recursion.
- Recursive Case reduces the problem size.
- Every recursive call is stored in the Call Stack.
- Recursion is widely used in Trees, Graphs, DP, and Backtracking.

